      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "preamplifier",
        "description": "NE5532 dual op-amp used as the low-level preamplifier stage operating from the external single 9V supply. This module receives the external low-level audio input, provides the primary voltage gain needed toward the overall target of about 100x-200x, and drives the downstream LM386 power amplifier input. One NE5532 channel should be used as the active preamplifier signal path; the second channel remains available for auxiliary buffering, bias generation support, or should be placed in a defined unused-state network if not required. Because only VCC_P and VCC_N power pins are provided and the brief requires single-supply operation, this module depends on an external passive bias/reference network to establish the op-amp signal operating point within the 9V domain. This module is the owner of the analog small-signal path into the power amplifier and should keep its gain-setting and biasing network local to preserve low-noise behavior.",
        "id": "preamplifier"
      },
