      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "power_amplifier",
        "description": "LM386 low-voltage audio power amplifier used as the final output stage from the external single 9V supply. This module receives the preamplified analog signal from the NE5532 stage, applies the final stage voltage gain and power drive, and delivers the amplified audio output suitable for an 8-ohm speaker load. IN_POS is the intended signal input interface, while IN_NEG should be configured according to the standard single-ended LM386 application topology during downstream wiring. GAIN_1 and GAIN_2 are available and should be configured by the later passive network to set the LM386 stage gain so that the full amplifier chain meets the overall gain target without overcommitting the NE5532 stage alone. BYPASS is available for noise and bias stabilization intent. This module is the owner of the high-current audio output path and should keep output return routing and supply decoupling arranged to limit coupling back into the low-level preamplifier stage.",
        "id": "power_amplifier"
